course: dictionary
lesson: 13470
title: Hydration
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Hydration is a noun, which means it names a thing. Its main meaning is taking in enough water so that your body works well. «Remember to keep up your hydration on hot days.» Here it means drinking enough water.
explain: Hydration can also mean putting water or moisture into something dry, such as skin or soil. «The gardener checked the hydration of the soil before planting the seeds.» The soil needs water, so the word means how wet it is, or how much water it has.
explain: Read the words around hydration to find its meaning. Look for clues like water, drink, bottle, soil or body. «After the match, Sam drank two bottles of water for good hydration.» The word water tells you hydration is about drinking.
fact: Hydration is a noun, and it is uncountable, so you say good hydration, not a hydration.
fact: «Hydration» means taking in enough water so that your body works well.
fact: «Hydration» can also mean adding water or moisture to something, such as skin, soil or a dry substance.
fact: In chemistry, «hydration» is a reaction in which water joins with another substance. Cement sets by hydration.
fact: Useful phrases: a hydration pack, a hydration station, and to stay on top of your hydration.
exercise: «Sam filled his water bottle before the match to keep good hydration.» What does hydration mean here? | *Taking in enough water so the body works well | Sleeping well at night | Eating a big lunch | Wearing a warm jacket
exercise: The gardener checked the soil's hydration before planting. What does hydration mean here? | The name of a garden tool | *How much water or moisture the soil has | The colour of the soil | How deep the hole is
exercise: «At school, the hydration station is where you refill your water bottle.» What is a hydration station? | A place to buy new shoes | *A place where you can get water to drink | A room for maths lessons | A gym for lifting weights
test: Coach says, «Stay on top of your hydration.» What should you do? | *Keep drinking enough water during the day | Run faster than everyone else | Wear more layers of clothing | Go to bed early every night
test: In chemistry, hydration is a reaction where | Water turns into steam | A substance turns into a gas | A substance loses all its water | *Water joins with another substance
exam: Which sentence uses hydration to mean adding moisture? | «The hydration station is closed today.» | «Sam drank water for good hydration.» | *«The gardener improved the hydration of the dry soil.» | «Ella packed a hydration pack for the hike.»
